WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.784 --> 00:00:17.774
The next morning Anne realized that Matthew was not looking well.

2
00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:22.238
After he had left, Anne said, "Marilla, is Matthew well?"

3
00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:25.580
"No," said Marilla in a troubled tone.

4
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.764
"His heart has been quite bad this spring, but he keeps working.

5
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.042
Maybe he'll rest now that you're home.

6
00:00:32.622 --> 00:00:34.324
You always cheer him up."

7
00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:36.305
Anne looked at Marilla.

8
00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:38.847
"You're not looking well yourself, Marilla.

9
00:00:39.548 --> 00:00:41.590
You must rest, now that I'm home."

10
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.512
Marilla smiled affectionately at her girl.

11
00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:47.394
"It's not the work, it's my eyes.

12
00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:49.616
I'm seeing an optometrist soon."

13
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.379
In the evening Anne went to see Matthew in the fields.

14
00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.022
Matthew walked slowly with his head down.

15
00:00:56.042 --> 00:01:00.137
"You've been working too hard, Matthew," she said reproachfully.

16
00:01:00.157 --> 00:01:03.238
"I forget I'm getting older," Matthew replied.

17
00:01:03.258 --> 00:01:08.021
"If I'd been the boy you sent for," said Anne, "I could help you."

18
00:01:08.041 --> 00:01:11.623
"Anne, I'd rather have you than a dozen boys.

19
00:01:12.343 --> 00:01:14.445
It wasn't a boy who got that scholarship.

20
00:01:15.085 --> 00:01:17.946
It was a girl, my girl, whom I'm proud of."

21
00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:21.568
Later that night Anne remembered Matthew's words.

22
00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:27.912
It was the last night before sorrow touched Anne's life, and no life is quite the same afterward.

23
00:01:28.476 --> 00:01:30.277
"Matthew, what is the matter?"

24
00:01:30.918 --> 00:01:33.700
It was Marilla who spoke, holding Matthew's head.

25
00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.681
Anne burst through the door.

26
00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:39.183
"He's fainted," gasped Marilla.

27
00:01:39.203 --> 00:01:41.485
"Anne, run for Martin.

28
00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:48.190
Quick!" Martin was the hired man, and he drove to get the doctor, stopping at the Lyndes' house

29
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.330
to tell them the news.

30
00:01:50.051 --> 00:01:52.072
Mrs. Lynde came as quickly as she could.

31
00:01:52.693 --> 00:01:57.396
She pushed Anne and Marilla gently aside and then laid her ear on Matthew's heart.

32
00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:00.397
She looked at their anxious faces sorrowfully.

33
00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:03.298
"Oh, Marilla," she said gravely.

34
00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:06.819
"I don't think we can do anything for him."

35
00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:09.159
Anne spoke quietly.

36
00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:15.921
"Mrs. Lynde, you don't think Matthew is is Anne could not say the dreadful word.

37
00:02:16.662 --> 00:02:18.402
She turned sick and pale.

38
00:02:19.102 --> 00:02:21.783
The doctor said Matthew's death had been painless.

39
00:02:22.523 --> 00:02:28.277
The news spread quickly through Avonlea, and all day friends and neighbors came to pay their respects.

40
00:02:29.118 --> 00:02:30.798
That night the house was quiet.

41
00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:33.640
Matthew's death left a horrible ache.

42
00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.921
When Anne sobbed, Marilla came to comfort her.

43
00:02:36.941 --> 00:02:39.302
"What will we do without him?"

44
00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:40.342
Anne cried.

45
00:02:40.362 --> 00:02:43.864
"We've got each other, Anne," Marilla said softly.

46
00:02:43.884 --> 00:02:47.965
"I don't know what I'd do if you weren't here—if you'd never come."

47
00:02:49.186 --> 00:02:52.527
Slowly life went on, and work was done as before.

48
00:02:53.307 --> 00:02:59.295
Anne, new to grief, thought this was sad—that they could go on in the old way without Matthew.

49
00:03:00.035 --> 00:03:02.997
She felt almost ashamed that she could feel happy again.

50
00:03:03.697 --> 00:03:07.519
She missed him so much, and yet the world still seemed beautiful.

51
00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:08.600
But Mrs.

52
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.742
Lynde assured her, "Matthew would want you to be happy, Anne.

53
00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:14.963
He liked to hear you laugh."

54
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:19.606
"I saw Gilbert Blythe today," Marilla said one afternoon.

55
00:03:19.626 --> 00:03:23.328
"What a nice-looking fellow he is," she went on.

56
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.621
"He's so tall and manly.

57
00:03:26.162 --> 00:03:28.724
He looks a lot like his father did at the same age.

58
00:03:29.344 --> 00:03:31.126
We used to be very good friends.

59
00:03:31.766 --> 00:03:33.628
People called him my boyfriend."

60
00:03:34.268 --> 00:03:35.629
Anne looked up with interest.

61
00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.771
"Oh Marilla, what happened?"

62
00:03:37.791 --> 00:03:40.734
"We had a fight," Marilla said.

63
00:03:40.754 --> 00:03:44.937
"I wouldn't forgive him right away; I wanted to punish him first.

64
00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.698
He never came back.

65
00:03:47.339 --> 00:03:49.381
The Blythes were very independent.

66
00:03:50.001 --> 00:03:53.364
But I've always wished I'd forgiven him when I had the chance."

67
00:03:54.144 --> 00:03:58.327
"So you've had a bit of romance in your life too," said Anne softly.

68
00:03:58.347 --> 00:03:59.908
"Yes, I guess.

69
00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:02.410
You wouldn't know from looking at me!

70
00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.652
But you can never tell people from their outsides."

71
00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:10.495
The next day Anne came home to find Marilla looking dejected.

72
00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:12.397
"Are you tired, Marilla?"

73
00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:17.780
"Yes no I don't know," said Marilla wearily.

74
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.201
"It's not that."

75
00:04:19.221 --> 00:04:21.443
"Did you see the optometrist?"

76
00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:23.104
asked Anne anxiously.

77
00:04:24.288 --> 00:04:26.330
"Yes, I saw him," said Marilla.

78
00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:33.136
"He said if I wear glasses and stop reading and sewing, my eyes will be all right.

79
00:04:33.817 --> 00:04:36.939
But if I don't, I'll be blind in six months!

80
00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.643
Blind! Anne, just think of it."

81
00:04:40.663 --> 00:04:44.586
"Things have changed so much since I came home!"

82
00:04:45.087 --> 00:04:46.188
Anne thought sadly.

83
00:04:47.309 --> 00:04:50.972
One afternoon a few days later, Marilla came in from the yard.

84
00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.001
She had been talking to a man named Mr.

85
00:04:54.041 --> 00:05:00.564
Sadler. There were tears in Marilla's eyes, and her voice broke as she told Anne, "He heard I

86
00:05:00.604 --> 00:05:04.166
was going to sell Green Gables, and he wants to buy it."

87
00:05:05.006 --> 00:05:06.386
"Buy Green Gables?"

88
00:05:06.887 --> 00:05:07.707
Anne burst out.

89
00:05:07.727 --> 00:05:10.868
"Marilla, are you selling Green Gables?"

90
00:05:10.888 --> 00:05:14.630
"If my eyes were strong, I could stay here.

91
00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.652
But I may lose my sight, and I can't stay here alone.

92
00:05:19.348 --> 00:05:22.309
Mrs. Lynde advised me to sell and stay with her.

93
00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:33.514
I'm sorry you won't have a home to come to on vacation Marilla broke down and wept bitterly.

94
00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:40.937
"You mustn't sell Green Gables," said Anne firmly, "and you won't stay here alone, Marilla.

95
00:05:41.597 --> 00:05:42.497
I'll be with you."

96
00:05:43.138 --> 00:05:45.479
Marilla looked at Anne, "What do you mean?"

97
00:05:45.499 --> 00:05:48.580
"I'm not taking the scholarship.

98
00:05:49.152 --> 00:05:51.473
I couldn't leave you after all you've done for me.

99
00:05:52.113 --> 00:05:56.815
The Avonlea School is promised to Gilbert Blythe, but I can teach in Carmody.

100
00:05:57.515 --> 00:05:58.996
I won't leave you, Marilla."

101
00:05:59.696 --> 00:06:00.877
Marilla was stunned.

102
00:06:00.897 --> 00:06:04.478
"But I can't let you sacrifice your education for me."

103
00:06:04.498 --> 00:06:08.520
"Nonsense, there is no sacrifice!"

104
00:06:10.221 --> 00:06:10.901
Anne laughed.

105
00:06:11.741 --> 00:06:14.402
"Nothing could be worse than giving up Green Gables.

106
00:06:15.203 --> 00:06:18.164
I'll be a good teacher—and save your eyesight.

107
00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:21.487
Besides, I'll study college courses at home."

108
00:06:21.507 --> 00:06:26.571
"I feel as if you've given me a new life," Marilla said, beaming.

109
00:06:27.552 --> 00:06:33.658
In Avonlea people heard that Anne had given up the idea of going to university and, not knowing

110
00:06:33.718 --> 00:06:36.000
about Marilla's eyes, thought she was foolish.

111
00:06:36.681 --> 00:06:37.161
But Mrs.

112
00:06:37.261 --> 00:06:41.105
Lynde told Anne, "I'm glad to hear you're not going, Anne.

113
00:06:41.826 --> 00:06:44.188
I don't believe in women going to university."

114
00:06:44.728 --> 00:06:48.150
"But I'll teach at Carmody and study Latin and Greek at home, Mrs.

115
00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.731
Lynde!" said Anne laughing.

116
00:06:50.751 --> 00:06:54.453
"The school board gave you Avonlea School," Mrs.

117
00:06:54.533 --> 00:06:55.134
Lynde said.

118
00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.335
Anne jumped to her feet.

119
00:06:57.355 --> 00:06:59.876
"I thought they promised it to Gilbert Blythe!"

120
00:07:00.777 --> 00:07:01.697
"They did.

121
00:07:02.397 --> 00:07:08.961
But when Gilbert heard you applied, he withdrew his application and suggested you for the job.

122
00:07:09.621 --> 00:07:11.682
He is going to teach at White Sands.

123
00:07:12.363 --> 00:07:14.464
Wasn't that kind and thoughtful of him?"

124
00:07:15.136 --> 00:07:16.616
"Gilbert did that for me?"

125
00:07:17.037 --> 00:07:17.717
Anne murmured.

126
00:07:18.557 --> 00:07:24.419
At dusk Anne went to the little Avonlea graveyard and put fresh flowers on Matthew's grave.

127
00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:27.939
She lingered there, liking the peace of the place.

128
00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.940
A tall man came toward her, whistling.

129
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.061
"Gilbert!" Anne said, her cheeks flushed.

130
00:07:34.081 --> 00:07:36.842
"Thank you for giving up the school for me."

131
00:07:37.862 --> 00:07:39.643
Gilbert took her hand eagerly.

132
00:07:39.663 --> 00:07:41.063
"That's all right, Anne.

133
00:07:41.643 --> 00:07:42.964
Are we going to be friends after this?

134
00:07:43.464 --> 00:07:44.444
Have you really forgiven me?"

135
00:07:45.124 --> 00:07:45.784
Anne laughed.

136
00:07:45.804 --> 00:07:51.766
"I forgave you the day you rescued me from the brook, although I didn't know it."

137
00:07:52.406 --> 00:07:57.207
When Anne came home later, Marilla asked curiously, "Who was with you, Anne?"

138
00:07:57.227 --> 00:08:01.228
"Gilbert Blythe," answered Anne, blushing.

139
00:08:01.249 --> 00:08:02.769
"He walked with me."

140
00:08:02.789 --> 00:08:06.210
"I didn't think you two were such good friends."

141
00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:07.890
Marilla smiled.

142
00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:11.071
"We've been good enemies," said Anne.

143
00:08:11.091 --> 00:08:13.572
"But it's more sensible to be friends."

144
00:08:14.436 --> 00:08:16.800
Anne sat at her window that night, content.

145
00:08:17.522 --> 00:08:23.191
Green Gables was her home, and the dreams of a little redheaded orphan girl had come true.
